title <b>Deployment Flow Diagram</b>\nPrompt Guard in the Backend Request Pipeline

actor "User" as User
participant "Web UI\n(Frontend)" as UI
participant "FastAPI\nBackend" as API
participant "prompt_guard\nPromptScanner" as PG
participant "Risk Scoring\nEngine" as SCORING
participant "Audit DB\n& Logger" as DB
participant "LLM Service\n(External)" as LLM

== Standard Repo Scan Flow (unchanged) ==

User -> UI : Submit GitHub URL
UI -> API : POST /scan { repo_url }
API -> API : clone_repository()
API -> API : detect_languages()
API -> API : run 10 parallel scanners\n(Semgrep, Bandit, ESLint, ...)
API -> API : normalise_all(findings)
API --> UI : ScanResponse (findings JSON)

|||

== Prompt Security Flow (NEW — Prompt Guard) ==

User -> UI : Submit prompt / query
UI -> API : POST /prompt/analyze { prompt }

group Prompt Guard Intercept Layer
  API -> PG : scan(prompt, config)

  group Analysis Pipeline
    PG -> PG : normalize_text(prompt)
    PG -> PG : has_suspicious_encoding()
    PG -> PG : StaticAnalyzer.analyze()
    PG -> PG : HeuristicAnalyzer.analyze()
    PG -> PG : SemanticAnalyzer.analyze()
    PG -> PG : _deduplicate_findings()
  end

  PG -> SCORING : calculate_risk_score(findings)
  SCORING --> PG : risk_score, risk_level
  PG --> API : ScanResult(safe, risk_score, findings, recommendations)
end

API -> DB : audit_log(prompt_hash, scan_result)

alt safe == True (risk_score below threshold)
  API -> LLM : Forward prompt
  LLM --> API : LLM response text
  API --> UI : HTTP 200\n{ response, scan_metadata }
  note right of API
    scan_metadata includes:
    • risk_score (e.g. 12.5)
    • risk_level: LOW
    • scan_time_seconds
  end note

else safe == False (risk_score at/above threshold)
  API -[#CC0000]-> UI : HTTP 200\n{ safe: false, findings[], recommendations[] }
  note right of API #FFE0E0
    Prompt BLOCKED.
    LLM is never called.
    Findings detail why:
    e.g. "jailbreak_attempt [HIGH]"
  end note
end

|||
== Deployment Environment ==

note over API, PG
  <b>Same Process — Same Container</b>
  prompt_guard is installed as a Python package
  alongside the FastAPI backend.
  No additional service or network hop required.
  Latency overhead: ~5–50 ms per scan (measured).
end note

@enduml
